        ["Which statement BEST describes the Jimmo v. Sebelius settlement?",["Skilled maintenance therapy can be covered without improvement","Medicare stops paying once a patient stops making progress","Therapy is covered only after a three-day hospital stay","Maintenance programs must be performed only by aides"],"The Jimmo settlement clarified there is no improvement standard; skilled therapy to maintain function or slow decline can be covered when a therapist's skill is needed."],
        ["A hospitalized 84-year-old can walk with supervision but spends most of each day in bed. Which strategy BEST reduces her risk of hospital-associated disability?",["Scheduled walks and out-of-bed meals","Bed rest until the day of discharge","Bedside ankle pumps as the only activity","Delaying PT until outpatient follow-up"],"Frequent mobility and time out of bed counter the rapid deconditioning caused by bed rest. Waiting for discharge allows strength and function to decline."]
